MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Raising pp makes a high dp unreachable, and the row was dropping those entries
— so moving pp from 1 to 2 shortened the dp list and dragged the pp values
sideways under the cursor, which made the digits hard to track while adjusting
them.

Render every value each axis can take and strike through the ones the current
partner value rules out. The row keeps a constant width, so only the brackets
move, and the struck-out entries also make the constraint visible instead of
silently hiding options.

