Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three fixes to the status line, all so it tells the truth about the NPU
cards after a router restart or an eviction:

- The backend's default model (e.g. gpt-oss-120b from OPENAI_MODEL) no
  longer sits in the list red on every launch. npuDisplayModels now shows
  the current model only when it is actually live, transitioning, or
  remembered — not merely because it is the selected default.

- Models that were loaded before but are gone now show in red instead of
  vanishing. A new npuRecentModels store persists, per router base URL,
  which models have been seen `up`; the status line unions those with the
  live set and colours each by its real current state. So after the server
  is cleared, the models you were just using reappear red (not green), and
  you can arrow-key back to one to reload it. Every filesystem touch is
  guarded — a bad read or full disk must never break polling.

- The footer ←/→ selection and the `/model` colouring both read the same
  unioned list, so the cursor never lands on an invisible row.

Verified on live 4-card hardware end to end: two models loaded show green
and are remembered; after killing their serve processes the router reaps
them and the same two reappear red on the next launch; the default model
is absent throughout.

