From 04d6b86964adcf6e223c25e3786e8f0c0b823049 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunjun1234 <plab2090@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:20:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 14/23] model picker: add tp as a third parallel axis
 (tp/dp/pp)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Furiosa router now publishes multiple tp builds per model — a tp8 v2
artifact (1 card, pp-adjustable) alongside the default tp32 fxb build —
advertised as `@tp{N}` ids plus a new FURIO_NPU_META map
(base -> {tp_default, tps}) so the bare id's numeric tp is known.

- npuVariants: NpuVariant gains tp; parse/compose the `@tp` suffix via the
  meta map; generalize npuAxisValues/stepNpuAxis/npuAxisAllValues to three
  axes and add availableAxes/nextAxis. Stepping tp re-fits dp/pp (collapse
  to 1 on a whole-card build, keep otherwise); dp/pp hold tp and repair the
  partner. Falls back to dp/pp-only when no tp metadata is present.
- ModelPicker: npuConfig carries optional tp; tab cycles tp/dp/pp among
  adjustable axes; NpuParallelismRow renders the tp row only when the model
  has more than one build.
- tests: tp round-trip, axis values, tp32-collapse / tp8-keep, @tp compose.
