 polling on long loads
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two fixes for the Furiosa NPU workflow:

1. Runtime metadata. Discovery now also pulls /router/models and installs its
   descriptions + tp/pp metadata as the live source of truth (setRuntimeNpuMeta
   / setRuntimeDescriptions), winning over the install-time env vars. A
   router-side change (new model, different dp/pp/tp choices, pp default) then
   applies on the next launch without re-running install.sh. Non-Furiosa
   backends 404 and keep the env fallbacks. getBackendModelDescriptions is now
   cached on its raw string like npuMeta (it is read once per render).

2. Status-line polling backs off. While a model loads we poll every 1s so the
   LED tracks reality, but a big model can load for a minute or two and every
   poll repaints the whole TUI — which made the terminal feel sluggish after a
   /model pick. Keep 1s for the first 12s, then 4s, so the LED still moves
   without hammering the screen.
---
 src/services/npuStatus.ts               | 23 +++++++++--
 src/utils/model/openaiModelDiscovery.ts | 51 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
