Three fixes for the Furiosa NPU UI:

1. A single failed probe no longer disables the status line for the whole
   session. pollOnce now distinguishes a real HTTP response that is not a
   router status ('not-router' — OpenAI/Ollama, stop for good, as before) from
   a timeout or connection error ('unreachable' — the SSH tunnel reconnecting
   or the router restarting). Only the former stops polling. Previously any
   first-probe failure set `stopped`, leaving `available` false, and
   BuiltinStatusLine renders nothing at all in that state — so the per-model
   LEDs and the multi-model row silently vanished for the rest of the session,
   and a preload had no visible effect.

2. Idle polls no longer notify. `phase` is the blink clock, so a transition
   still ticks every poll, but when nothing is moving and nothing changed we
   skip the notify instead of repainting the whole TUI on every tick.

3. The model picker no longer re-renders on blink ticks. It subscribed to the
   full status, whose `models` array is new on every poll, so its memo missed
   and it rebuilt and repainted the entire option list once a second for the
   whole cold start of a model — exactly while the user is arrowing through it.
   New `useNpuLoadStates()` re-renders only when a model's id or state changes;
   the status line keeps using `useNpuStatus()` for the blink.
