From cc92ad4597ed6c0cf132cb5b81adf9367e3dea41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunjun1234 <plab2090@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:16:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] npu: cap the model switcher at four, ordered by when
 you picked them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ↓ switcher row grew with every model that had ever been loaded (up to the
eight the store keeps), so it wrapped the terminal and the ←/→ cursor had to
walk past models nobody was switching between.

- npuDisplayModels takes a limit (NPU_DISPLAY_LIMIT = 4, matching the card
  count) and now orders by pick recency: current model, then remembered
  newest-first, then anything live that was never picked here.
- recordNpuModelSelection() moves a model to the front when it is picked.
  rememberNpuModels() only sees what the router reports as up, in id order, so
  it cannot tell which of several live models was chosen last — the pick has to
  be recorded where it happens (preloadNpuModel, which every pick funnels
  through).

Tests: cap keeps the four newest, ordering follows picks not ids, the selected
model keeps its slot at the cap, a live-but-never-picked model still shows while
there is room; and for the store, a pick moves to front / does not duplicate /
survives a reload. Verified live: six seeded picks render as four.
