From: hyunjun1234 <plab2090@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:58:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] npu: Enter on the switcher loads the model, even the
 one already selected
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With nothing on the cards, opening the ↓ switcher puts the cursor on the model
you are already using (that is what ▶ marks), so Enter on it was the whole
interaction — and it did nothing. The branch was guarded by
`target !== npuCurrentModelId`, which skipped the preload along with the model
switch. Exactly the case where the user most needs the load to start.

Enter means "put this model on the cards", not "change the setting". Split those:
preload unconditionally, guard only the switch, since re-selecting the model you
already have would just churn settings and state.

Verified against a stub router reporting nothing loaded: ↓ then Enter on the ▶
entry posts /router/preload for that model and the LED goes to loading.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Na71jMPNwVCJecN1VMjJbo
